SUMMARY:Blindsight - Peter Watts
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everybody\,\n\nThanks for your patien
 ce while I got this month's announcement out. The good news is that\, sinc
 e we're meeting on the fourth Sunday this month\, you still have about fou
 r weeks to finish the book.\n\nOur August selection is the winner of the C
 ontemporary Sci-Fi survey! Based on your votes\, we'll be reading a mix of
  mysteries\, alien encounters\, planetary escapes\, and interplanetary tra
 vel over the coming months. I'm excited to see what connections we can dra
 w between these modern favorites and classic novels.\n\n*Blindsight* has b
 ecome something of a modern sci-fi classic. It's known for being smart\, s
 uspenseful\, and genuinely unsettling. Without giving too much away\, the 
 story follows a crew sent to investigate a mysterious alien presence at th
 e edge of our solar system. This should be a fun one!\n\nBook of the Month
 \n*Blindsight* \\- Peter Watts \\(2006\\)\n\n**Content warning:** *Blindsi
 ght* has horror elements and can get dark. If that's not your thing\, keep
  it in mind before jumping in. That said\, you can always skip ahead : )\n
 \n*Reactor* has a nice [summary and review here.](https://reactormag.com/c
 redible-creatures-in-space-peter-watts-blindsight/) Heads up for spoilers 
 in the article\, but worth a read when you're done. It’s a story about a
 n eclectic crew aboard an ion-eating ship\, a strange signal\, and a terri
 fying mystery.\n\nYou can buy it online\, at your bookstore\, listen via a
 udiobook\, or [DOWNLOAD THE PDF HERE FOR FREE](chrome-extension://efaidnbm
 nnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://www.rifters.com/real/shorts/PeterWatts_Bl
 indsight.pdf) from the author's website. *Not spam\, I promise.* Watts ini
 tially self-published this novel and had it free online.\n\nTo join a Book
  Club meeting\, all you will need is YOURSELF. If you haven’t had a chan
 ce to finish the book\, we still would love for you to join us in the disc
 ussion.\n\nNot able to join us in person for events? [The Sci Fi Book Club
  is on Discord](https://discord.gg/B9NMnC2F). Join us and keep the convers
 ation going.
